---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { docs, repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Architecture | OrbitKV"
  description="OrbitKV attention-state compilation, ownership, token-level reclamation, and adapter boundaries."
  active="Architecture"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
    <h1>One authority for snapshots, sharing, and reuse.</h1>
    <p>
      OrbitKV is an attention-state compiler and transactional ownership
      runtime. ABI8 turns retention semantics into immutable snapshots, exact
      physical intents, and completion-gated reclamation while engines retain
      their execution responsibilities.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Architecture" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Pipeline</h2>
      <pre><code>{`Attention and state-retention semantics
    -> checked retention IR
    -> lifetime classes and address programs
    -> immutable request snapshot
    -> exact copy and write intents
    -> adapter completion evidence
    -> publication and reclamation ACK`}</code></pre>

      <h2>Ownership boundary</h2>
      <table class="evidence-table-native">
        <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Authority</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>OrbitKV</td><td>Plans, identities, generations, snapshots, references, transactions, and reuse decisions</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Adapter</td><td>Checked tensor effects, mirror updates, and exact completion evidence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Engine</td><td>Allocation, scheduling, kernels, execution, and request protocol</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Safety invariants</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Logical identity is separate from physical slot and generation.</li>
        <li>Immutable snapshot heads are the ownership authority; adapter mirrors are not.</li>
        <li>Unsupported semantics and engine contracts fail closed before mutation.</li>
        <li>Ambiguous post-mutation outcomes fail stop instead of guessing ownership.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Semantic and execution frontiers</h2>
      <p>
        Token-level reclamation requires two independent proofs. The Semantic
        Frontier shows that a logical token is no longer reachable from live
        snapshots. The Execution Frontier shows that prior device work can no
        longer read or write its storage. A page becomes reusable only after
        both proofs and the exact backend acknowledgement are present.
      </p>
      <p>
        Relocation packs retained tokens out of partially dead pages. It is
        byte-exact state movement and physical reclamation, not numerical
        compression or an automatic capacity benefit.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing and packed copy-on-write</h2>
      <p>
        Prefix references and request forks share immutable roots. Extending a
        shared or pinned partial tail creates an exact COW intent; publication
        waits until the adapter proves the copy completed before new writes.
        Packed fork and shared partial-tail COW have ABI8 host coverage. Packed
        Prefix and broader device qualification remain pending.
      </p>

      <h2>Engine-neutral adapter</h2>
      <p>
        The adapter SPI describes append, copy, clear, completion, and mirror
        cleanup as typed effects. The reference external arena is a contract
        oracle, not a scheduler, model runner, kernel library, or serving
        engine. An integration inherits no qualification from another adapter.
      </p>

      <h2>Evidence boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The compiler and ownership core have broad ABI8 host gates. Sealed
        engine records cover separate, narrow Prefix and token-relocation
        correctness/lifecycle scopes; their claims do not transfer. Other state
        families and execution modes retain narrower or pending coverage.
        Performance and production qualification remain pending. Historical
        records remain evidence only for their recorded ABI and source closure.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/capability-matrix.md`}>Capability Matrix</a>{" "}
        is normative. Detailed manifests and methods belong in the{" "}
        <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/results/README.md`}>Results Index</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Reference documents</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        {docs.map((item) => (
          <div class="doc-card">
            <span>{item.key}</span>
            <h3>{item.name}</h3>
            <p>{item.detail}</p>
            <a href={item.href}>Open document →</a>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
